	'nl_label' => '(The letter)',
	'p_about_intro' => 'Founded in 2014, Yuzuriha Retreat is a residential lodge for yoga, forest walks, and plain meals in Fernhollow Valley. We host twelve guests at a time in a restored former forestry hostel.',
	'p_about_k' => '(About) · Since 2014',
	'p_about_s1_b' => 'Yuzuriha Retreat opened in 2014 within a former forestry hostel situated at Larch Hill Lane 9 in Fernhollow Valley. The building had stood empty after decades of housing forestry teams working among the surrounding larches and pines. Ines Calloway established the retreat to offer an unhurried sanctuary centered on daily yoga, woodland walking, and wholesome food. In 2018, we expanded the lodge by constructing our timber practice hall, measuring 14 by 9 meters, designed specifically to capture soft northern daylight through tall forest windows. Today, the property operates from March to November each year, closing from December through February when winter snow isolates the high ridge paths.',
	'p_about_s1_h' => 'From a Forestry Hostel to a Quiet Lodge',
	'p_about_s2_b' => 'We deliberately keep every retreat capped at twelve guests. This number ensures that the house remains peaceful from dawn until nightfall, without crowded hallways or bustling schedules. Twelve guests fit comfortably across our eight bedrooms, comprising four single rooms and four twin rooms. At meal times, twelve chairs surround our single long dining table where everyone shares breakfast, lunch, and supper together. During morning and evening sessions, each person enjoys ample floor space on the timber floor of the practice hall or across the covered deck that looks out directly over the falling forest slope.',
	'p_about_s2_h' => 'Why We Welcome Only Twelve Guests',
	'p_about_s3_b' => 'We believe quiet structure is more beneficial than rigid prescription. We make no detox claims, offer no medical therapies, and stage no ceremonial performances. There is no television on the property, and we do not police your electronic devices. Instead, we simply ask that phones rest quietly in a woven basket by the practice hall door before morning and evening practice, a custom that is gently requested but never enforced. Our guests are people who are tired from modern haste rather than unwell, seeking three to seven days where nothing complicated needs to be decided.',
	'p_about_s3_h' => 'What Practices Do We Leave Out at the Lodge?',
	'p_about_t' => 'About Yuzuriha Retreat',
	'p_calendar_intro' => 'We host four residential retreat formats between March and November each year. Each retreat is strictly limited to twelve guests to preserve a calm and spacious atmosphere.',
	'p_calendar_k' => '(Calendar) · 2027',
	'p_calendar_s1_b' => 'Our 2027 calendar includes eight scheduled retreats during the spring and early summer season. The Three-Day First Light Retreat runs 12 to 14 March and 23 to 25 April at €540 per person. The Five-Day Forest Retreat takes place 22 to 26 March and 10 to 14 May at €920 per person. The Seven-Day Quiet Retreat is held 4 to 10 April and 6 to 12 June at €1,280 per person. The Weekend Walking Retreat is scheduled for 7 to 9 May and 18 to 20 June at €480 per person. Every date accommodates twelve guests.',
	'p_calendar_s1_h' => 'Our 2027 Retreat Dates',
	'p_calendar_s2_b' => 'In March 2027, we host First Light from 12 to 14 March for €540, followed by the Five-Day Forest Retreat from 22 to 26 March for €920. In April, Sun-hee Park leads the Seven-Day Quiet Retreat from 4 to 10 April for €1,280, followed by First Light from 23 to 25 April for €540. In May, we offer the Weekend Walking Retreat from 7 to 9 May for €480 and the Forest Retreat from 10 to 14 May for €920. In June, we conclude the spring season with the Quiet Retreat from 6 to 12 June for €1,280 and Weekend Walking from 18 to 20 June for €480.',
	'p_calendar_s2_h' => 'Dates by Month from March to June',
	'p_calendar_s3_b' => 'Dates for retreats taking place between July and November are published exclusively in our January seasonal letter. We keep our schedule structured in two seasonal releases so that past guests and newsletter readers receive early notice before spaces open widely. The lodge operates through November before closing for the winter months of December, January, and February. If you wish to join us during late summer or autumn, consider subscribing to our quarterly newsletter or writing directly to our reservations desk to register your interest.',
	'p_calendar_s3_h' => 'When Are Dates for July to November Released?',
	'p_calendar_t' => 'Retreat Calendar',
	'p_contact_intro' => 'Whether you have questions about retreat schedules, require driving directions, or wish to discuss whole-lodge hire, our team is here to assist you.',
	'p_contact_k' => '(Contact) · Monday–Saturday',
	'p_contact_s1_b' => 'For inquiries regarding retreat availability, room arrangements, or valley travel, contact our reservations desk directly. You can call us on +00 44 555 0186 or write by email to stay@yuzuriha.example. Nadia Haddad oversees all correspondence and answers inquiries Monday through Saturday from 09:00 to 17:00, replying within one working day. Our physical lodge is situated at Larch Hill Lane 9 in Fernhollow Valley. Because we run quiet residential retreats, we kindly ask that visitors make advance arrangements rather than dropping in unannounced.',
	'p_contact_s1_h' => 'Speaking with Our House Desk',
	'p_contact_s2_b' => 'We welcome visiting teachers and retreat organisers who wish to hire the entire property for their own private groups. Whole-lodge hire costs €2,400 per night and accommodates up to twelve guests across our eight bedrooms, comprising four single and four twin rooms. Organisers have exclusive access to our 14 by 9 meter timber practice hall, the forest deck, and all grounds. Mateo Ruiz provides three plain daily meals from our kitchen, while Tomas Eklund manages heating and van transfers. Whole-lodge bookings require a minimum stay of three nights.',
	'p_contact_s2_h' => 'Whole-Lodge Hire for Teachers and Organisers',
	'p_contact_s3_b' => 'Journalists, architectural publications, and media writers seeking information or documentary photography regarding Yuzuriha Retreat should send inquiries to stay@yuzuriha.example with the subject line clearly marked as press enquiry. Nadia reviews all editorial requests during regular desk hours from Monday to Saturday, 09:00 to 17:00. We maintain a collection of high-resolution film-grain photographs documenting our timber building, forest surroundings, and daily routine that can be provided to approved publications upon request.',
	'p_contact_s3_h' => 'How Should Media and Press Inquiries Reach Us?',
	'p_contact_t' => 'Contact Us',
	'p_getting_here_intro' => 'Yuzuriha Retreat is located at Larch Hill Lane 9 in Fernhollow Valley. We are accessible by train via Fernhollow station or by private automobile along valley roads.',
	'p_getting_here_k' => '(Getting here) · Fernhollow Valley',
	'p_getting_here_s1_b' => 'If arriving by train, book your journey to Fernhollow station. Our lodge van meets incoming guests directly outside the station doors at 14:30 on arrival day, making the twenty-five minute drive up into the valley in time for 16:00 welcome tea. On departure day, the return van leaves the lodge at 14:00 to connect with afternoon rail departures. Guests traveling by car will find on-site parking for eight vehicles. Please note that while valley approach highways are paved, the final two kilometers along Larch Hill Lane consist of an unpaved gravel forestry road.',
	'p_getting_here_s1_h' => 'Arriving by Train or by Car',
	'p_getting_here_s2_b' => 'The retreat operates from March to November, each month bringing distinct mountain character. March brings snowmelt, brisk winds, and crisp air on the ridge. April introduces fresh mist, damp pine needles, and budding larch needles. May brings blooming valley wildflowers and rushing stream meltwater. June offers long daylight hours and dry mountain trails. July features fragrant pine warmth and cool forest shade. August brings warm afternoons and starry night skies. September turns the larch needles a brilliant golden yellow. October delivers crisp morning frosts and aromatic woodsmoke. November brings quiet woods and early winter dustings before our winter closure.',
	'p_getting_here_s2_h' => 'Fernhollow Valley Through the Seasons',
	'p_getting_here_s3_b' => 'Tomas Eklund drives our private lodge transfer van, ensuring guests reach the retreat smoothly without navigating mountain taxi services. The van is coordinated specifically around our 14:30 arrival window and our 14:00 departure schedule. Because the lodge is tucked deep in Fernhollow Valley where commercial ride services are unavailable, we strongly encourage rail travelers to time their train arrivals before 14:30. If your train experiences delays, please contact Nadia Haddad by telephone at +00 44 555 0186 as soon as possible so Tomas can adjust pickup arrangements accordingly.',
	'p_getting_here_s3_h' => 'How Does the Scheduled Van Transfer Work?',
	'p_getting_here_t' => 'Getting Here',
	'p_kitchen_intro' => 'Meals at Yuzuriha Retreat are plain, nourishing, and served family-style at our single long table. Cook Mateo Ruiz prepares three honest meals each day using seasonal ingredients.',
	'p_kitchen_k' => '(Kitchen) · Three plain meals',
	'p_kitchen_s1_b' => 'Our kitchen is run by Mateo Ruiz, who prepares three balanced, unpretentious meals each day for our twelve guests. Dining together at our single long table is central to life at the lodge, offering a natural space to talk, listen, or simply enjoy hot food in quiet companionship. Our food is primarily vegetarian, centered on wholesome grains, mountain vegetables, pulses, and hearty one-pot stews. Twice each week, Mateo introduces fresh fish to evening suppers. Every afternoon while guests rest or read, fresh sourdough bread rises in the kitchen to accompany the evening meal at 18:30.',
	'p_kitchen_s1_h' => 'Plain Meals at the Long Dining Table',
	'p_kitchen_s2_b' => 'Breakfast is served at 08:00 immediately following morning practice, offering warm porridges, toasted bread, fruit, and freshly brewed coffee. Lunch at 12:30 welcomes guests back from their forest walks with satisfying grain bowls, vegetable broths, and light savory dishes. Supper at 18:30 brings everyone back to the table for nourishing soups, baked fish or braised greens, and warm loaves broken by hand. Outside scheduled dining hours, hot herbal teas, filtered mountain water, and roasted barley infusions remain available at any hour on the kitchen sideboard and deck rail.',
	'p_kitchen_s2_h' => 'Breakfast, Lunch, and Hot Tea',
	'p_kitchen_s3_b' => 'We gladly adapt our cooking to suit vegan, gluten-free, and nut-free dietary requirements when notified in advance. Because all food is prepared fresh daily, please mention your specific dietary needs when sending your reservation request to Nadia. However, please note that our lodge operates one open kitchen without a segregated allergen preparation room. While Mateo takes diligent care when preparing allergen-aware dishes, an entirely trace-free environment cannot be maintained for individuals with severe or airborne food allergies. Feel free to contact our kitchen with specific questions before booking.',
	'p_kitchen_s3_h' => 'Can Dietary Requirements Be Accommodated?',
	'p_kitchen_t' => 'Kitchen and Meals',
	'p_newsletter_intro' => 'We publish a calm seasonal letter four times a year in January, April, July, and October. It contains our upcoming calendar, notes from the kitchen, and reflections from the forest.',
	'p_newsletter_k' => '(Letter) · Four a year',
	'p_newsletter_s1_b' => 'Our seasonal letter arrives four times a year, mailed at the turn of each season in January, April, July, and October. Rather than frequent promotional messages, we send a quiet bulletin that shares our operational plans and reflects the changing valley landscape. In the January letter, we publish the second half of our annual retreat calendar covering dates from July through November. Subscribers receive first opportunity to reserve places for these summer and autumn dates before they are announced more widely.',
	'p_newsletter_s1_h' => 'Four Letters Across the Seasons',
	'p_newsletter_s2_b' => 'Every quarterly letter contains three specific elements. First, you receive the confirmed schedule of upcoming retreats and early notice of newly opened dates or last-minute cancellation spaces. Second, Mateo Ruiz shares seasonal notes and simple recipes from our lodge kitchen, highlighting vegetable broths, bread-making tips, and warm evening stews. Third, Kofi Mensah contributes brief forest observations, describing trail conditions, bird migrations, and botanical changes along the 9 km larch ridge loop and the stream path.',
	'p_newsletter_s2_h' => 'What We Share in Each Issue',
	'p_newsletter_s3_b' => 'We treat your contact information with complete respect and discretion. When you subscribe using your email address, your details are stored privately and used solely to deliver our quarterly seasonal letter. We never sell, rent, or share your contact details with external commercial vendors or advertising networks. You can unsubscribe at any point with a single click or by sending a quick message to stay@yuzuriha.example, and your address will be removed immediately from our mailing records.',
	'p_newsletter_s3_h' => 'How Do We Protect Your Privacy?',
	'p_newsletter_t' => 'Quarterly Letter',
	'p_prices_intro' => 'All retreat fees include accommodation, every shared meal, and all daily yoga sessions and guided forest walks. There are no hidden service charges or equipment rental costs.',
	'p_prices_k' => '(Prices) · Euro, per person',
	'p_prices_s1_b' => 'The Three-Day First Light Retreat spans three days and two nights, featuring morning and evening yoga and two guided forest walks for €540. The Weekend Walking Retreat spans three days and two nights with three extended mountain walks and one daily yoga class for €480. The Five-Day Forest Retreat runs five days and four nights, providing the full daily rhythm of practice, ridge walks, and quiet hours for €920. The Seven-Day Quiet Retreat offers seven days and six nights of sustained restoration, featuring silent mornings until lunch led by Sun-hee Park for €1,280.',
	'p_prices_s1_h' => 'Four Retreat Formats Explained',
	'p_prices_s2_b' => 'Standard pricing covers twin-shared lodging, every meal, and all teaching. Guests requesting a private room pay a single room supplement of €35 per night across our four single bedrooms. Private sixty-minute sessions in yoga or guided walking can be added to any booked retreat for €60. Independent teachers and group organisers may also arrange whole-lodge hire for €2,400 per night for up to twelve guests, with a three-night minimum stay. Whole-lodge hire includes private use of all eight rooms, the practice hall, and three plain meals prepared daily by our kitchen.',
	'p_prices_s2_h' => 'Complete Price List and Private Hire',
	'p_prices_s3_b' => 'To secure a place on any retreat, we require a 30% deposit paid by bank transfer within five days of Nadia confirming availability. The remaining balance is due exactly 30 days before your retreat begins. If your circumstances change, your 30% deposit is refunded in full provided you notify us at least 45 days prior to arrival. Cancellations made fewer than 45 days before arrival forfeit the deposit. Payments are processed directly via bank transfer without booking surcharges or external platform fees.',
	'p_prices_s3_h' => 'How Do Deposits and Cancellations Work?',
	'p_prices_t' => 'Retreats and Prices',
	'p_reserve_intro' => 'We take reservations directly through our desk without third-party booking widgets or automated reservation engines. Nadia Haddad handles every booking personally by email.',
	'p_reserve_k' => '(Reserve) · One way, by email',
	'p_reserve_s1_b' => 'Reserving a retreat involves three simple steps. First, write an email to stay@yuzuriha.example stating your preferred retreat format, chosen dates, room preference of single or twin, and any dietary requirements. Second, Nadia reviews the lodge roster and replies within one working day, placing a temporary five-day hold on your requested room. Third, you confirm your booking by paying a 30% deposit via bank transfer. Once received, your place among the twelve guests is secured, and we send your complete arrival information pack.',
	'p_reserve_s1_h' => 'The Three Steps to Reserve Your Stay',
	'p_reserve_s2_b' => 'Paying your 30% deposit secures your room, while the remaining balance becomes due 30 days prior to your arrival date. We understand that plans can change unexpectedly. If you cancel your booking at least 45 days before your retreat commences, we refund your 30% deposit in full. Cancellations received under 45 days before arrival forfeit the deposit. Organisers booking whole-lodge hire for up to twelve guests pay €2,400 per night for a minimum of three nights, subject to the same deposit and cancellation schedule.',
	'p_reserve_s2_h' => 'Payment Schedules and Cancellation Terms',
	'p_reserve_s3_b' => 'Our house manager Nadia Haddad personally manages every inquiry and booking from our lodge office. The reservations desk operates Monday through Saturday from 09:00 to 17:00. You can reach Nadia directly by sending an email to stay@yuzuriha.example or by calling our desk at +00 44 555 0186 during regular office hours. Messages sent outside desk hours or on Sundays are answered promptly on the next working morning. Please include all relevant travel dates and guest details in your message.',
	'p_reserve_s3_h' => 'How Do You Contact the Reservations Desk?',
	'p_reserve_t' => 'Reserve a Place',
	'p_retreat_day_intro' => 'Every retreat follows a predictable rhythm shaped by daylight, shared practice, and honest meals. From the morning wake bell to evening quiet hours, the day unfolds without haste.',
	'p_retreat_day_k' => '(A retreat day) · 05:45–21:00',
	'p_retreat_day_s1_b' => 'The day begins at 05:45 with a single brass bell rung once along the corridor. At 06:15, guests gather for ninety minutes of morning practice led by Ines Calloway on the covered deck or in the timber hall. Breakfast is served at 08:00 around the long table. At 10:00, Kofi Mensah guides a two to three hour walk along the 9 km larch ridge loop or the sheltered 5 km stream path. Lunch follows at 12:30, giving way to afternoon rest, reading, or quiet conversation at 14:00. Hana Lindgren leads a gentle sixty minute restorative practice at 16:30, Mateo Ruiz serves supper at 18:30, and quiet hours settle across the lodge at 21:00.',
	'p_retreat_day_s1_h' => 'The Daily Rhythm from Morning to Night',
	'p_retreat_day_s2_b' => 'On arrival day, our caretaker Tomas Eklund meets guests at Fernhollow station at 14:30 in the lodge van for the twenty-five minute drive through the valley. Welcome tea is served on the deck at 16:00, allowing everyone to settle into their rooms before our first supper at 18:30. On departure day, we hold our final morning practice at 06:15, followed by a warm brunch at 10:00. Guests have time to pack and walk the grounds before the lodge van returns everyone to Fernhollow station at 14:00.',
	'p_retreat_day_s2_h' => 'Arrival and Departure Schedules',
	'p_retreat_day_s3_b' => 'You only need comfortable, practical clothing suited to mountain forest weather. We recommend warm wool or fleece layers, sturdy walking shoes or hiking boots for forest trails, and a refillable water bottle for daily walks. We supply all yoga equipment in the practice hall, including clean mats, wool blankets, and support blocks. Linens and towels are provided in every room. Because there are no laundry services on site, pack enough comfortable clothing for your full three to seven day retreat.',
	'p_retreat_day_s3_h' => 'What Should You Bring for Your Stay?',
	'p_retreat_day_t' => 'A Retreat Day',
	'p_rooms_intro' => 'Our lodge houses twelve guests across eight uncluttered bedrooms designed for deep rest. Natural timber, wool blankets, and forest views create a quiet atmosphere throughout the house.',
	'p_rooms_k' => '(Rooms) · 4 single, 4 twin',
	'p_rooms_s1_b' => 'The lodge offers eight bedrooms in total, divided equally into four single rooms and four twin rooms. Each bedroom is furnished with comfortable low timber beds dressed in pure linen sheets, warm wool blankets, and an adjustable reading lamp. In keeping with our restful ethos, there are no televisions or telephone sets anywhere in the guest rooms. Guests share three well-maintained bathrooms located along the central timber corridors. In the shared sitting area, a cast-iron wood stove tended daily by Tomas Eklund provides steady warmth and crackling cedar scent during cool valley mornings and chilly autumn evenings.',
	'p_rooms_s1_h' => 'Bedrooms and Living Spaces',
	'p_rooms_s2_b' => 'Our practice hall was built in 2018 and measures 14 by 9 meters. It features clean-grained timber floors, tall windows overlooking the canopy, and silent radiant floor heating. We store clean yoga mats, blocks, and folded wool blankets neatly along the wall for morning and evening practice. Adjoining the hall is our covered timber deck, elevated on sturdy posts directly over the sloping forest terrain. When morning weather is mild, Ines Calloway unrolls twelve mats along the deck boards so guests can practice in the fresh mountain air as mist rises through the valley larches.',
	'p_rooms_s2_h' => 'The Practice Hall and Forest Deck',
	'p_rooms_s3_b' => 'We have arranged the ground floor of the lodge to accommodate guests who prefer or require step-free access. Two of our ground-floor guest rooms provide level, step-free entry directly from the corridor, and the shared facilities on this level are arranged without steps. The covered forest deck and the outdoor sitting areas can be reached via a gently graded wooden ramp that connects directly to the main timber hallway. If you have mobility limitations or require ground-floor accommodation, please notify Nadia Haddad when submitting your reservation request.',
	'p_rooms_s3_h' => 'Is the Lodge Accessible for Step-Free Access?',
	'p_rooms_t' => 'Rooms and Facilities',
	'p_teachers_intro' => 'Seven people live and work at Yuzuriha Retreat, guiding daily practice, leading forest trails, tending the wood fire, and preparing your meals with steady, unhurried care.',
	'p_teachers_k' => '(Teachers) · Seven people',
	'p_teachers_s1_b' => 'Ines Calloway founded the retreat in 2014 and guides morning yoga practice at 06:15. At 05:50, she boils the kettle to carry twelve cups of hot tea to the deck before the wake bell rings. Hana Lindgren leads our evening restorative practice at 16:30, focusing on slow alignment, supported resting poses, and gentle nervous system release after active days outdoors. Sun-hee Park directs meditation and breathwork, guiding our Seven-Day Quiet Retreat with structured silent mornings until lunch. Kofi Mensah serves as our resident forest guide, leading guests through the 9 km larch ridge loop and the 5 km stream trail.',
	'p_teachers_s1_h' => 'Our Practice and Forest Guides',
	'p_teachers_s2_b' => 'Mateo Ruiz oversees the kitchen, cooking three plain meals a day that are vegetarian with fish twice weekly, while baking daily sourdough loaves during the afternoon rest. Nadia Haddad manages the reservations desk, responding to every guest booking and inquiry Monday through Saturday between 09:00 and 17:00 within one working day. Tomas Eklund serves as our resident caretaker, driving the lodge van between Fernhollow station and Larch Hill Lane, maintaining the forest paths, and keeping the cast-iron wood stove burning warmly throughout the cooler months from March to November.',
	'p_teachers_s2_h' => 'Our Kitchen and Household Caretakers',
	'p_teachers_s3_b' => 'Our teachers believe in patient, accessible guidance that accommodates both beginners and experienced practitioners. You do not need previous yoga experience or athletic conditioning to join our sessions. Ines and Hana provide clear physical modifications, using blocks and blankets to support every body safely. Sessions focus on mindful breath, natural spinal mobility, and calm awareness rather than physical strain or complicated choreography. We encourage you to move at your own comfort level, rest whenever necessary, and allow the quiet pace of the valley to restore your natural vitality.',
	'p_teachers_s3_h' => 'What Is the Teaching Philosophy at the Lodge?',
	'p_teachers_t' => 'Teachers and Team',
